event: sticky
data: {"bottomLineHtml":"<h2>BOTTOM LINE</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Verdict: HOLD — Medium conviction.</strong> Valuation (34.4x trailing / 39.6x fwd PE) already prices a multi-year growth reacceleration that isn't confirmed yet. Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a> · 2026-09-02.</li>\n<li><strong>Flip trigger:</strong> Confirmed AI/Services reacceleration (rev growth >18% YoY) at the Oct 28 print, or price pullback to ~$260-280 (28-30x fwd EPS).</li>\n<li><strong>12-mo price target: $350 (base), prob-weighted expected return ≈ +6%</strong> (see scenarios) — below what a growth mandate should demand from a new position.</li>\n<li><strong>Buy zone: $260–290. Do-not-chase above: $340.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Position size: 0–3% starter only on weakness</strong> — not a fresh full-size growth position at current price.</li></ul>","badges":{"recommendation":"HOLD","conviction":"Medium","sentiment":"Neutral"},"scorecardHtml":"<div class=\"scorecard\"><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Growth</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:70%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">7/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Moat</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:80%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">8/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Mgmt</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:60%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">6/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Value</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:30%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">3/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Balance</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:80%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">8/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Catalysts</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:60%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">6/10</span></div><div class=\"score-row\"><span class=\"score-label\">Overall</span><div class=\"score-bar\"><div class=\"score-fill\" style=\"width:60%\"></div></div><span class=\"score-num\">6/10</span></div></div>"}

event: body
data: {"html":"<h2>FUNDAMENTALS</h2>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>AAPL</th><th>Fact source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rev YoY / EPS YoY</td><td>16.36% / 29.13%</td><td>Fact · Yahoo 09/02/26</td></tr><tr><td>Gross/Op/Net margin</td><td>48.65% / 33.17% / 27.62%</td><td>Fact · Yahoo</td></tr><tr><td>PE / Fwd PE / PS / PB</td><td>34.36 / 39.55 / 9.49 / 50.98</td><td>Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL/key-statistics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stats</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul><li>Forward PE (39.6x) <strong>exceeds</strong> trailing PE (34.4x) — implied fwd EPS ≈ $8.23 vs trailing $9.47, a rare signal the Street models near-term EPS deceleration despite the strong Q1/Q2 FY26 beats. Fact · Yahoo.</li>\n<li><strong>Peer comp:</strong> MSFT 27.7x PE/11.1x PS; GOOGL 17.3x/9.5x; META 22.3x/6.6x — AAPL trades at the priciest earnings multiple in mega-cap tech despite similar/lower growth. Fact · Yahoo.</li>\n<li><strong>Reverse DCF:</strong> Implied TTM revenue = MktCap/PS = $4.75T/9.49 ≈ $500B; net income ≈ 27.6% × $500B ≈ $138B, matching PE math (14,687M sh × $9.47 EPS ≈ $139B). Using Price = NI/(r-g), r=9%: $4.75T/$138B=34.4 → r-g=2.9% → <strong>implied perpetual growth g≈6.1%</strong> baked into the price — demanding for a company this size over 12+ yrs.</li>\n<li><strong>FCF data not disclosed in feed</strong> (fcfPerShare/fcfMargin = null) — quality-of-earnings can't be fully verified; net-income proxy used above.</li>\n<li><strong>Capital return is thin:</strong> dividend yield 0.51%, payout ratio 12.1% — Apple returns very little via dividend; buyback/share-count trend is <strong>\"unknown\"</strong> in this feed (shareCountYoY null), so the historic buyback tailwind cannot be confirmed here. Fact · Yahoo.</li>\n<li><strong>Earnings history:</strong> 3 beats then 1 miss — Q1 FY26 +4.19%, Q2 +1.09%, Q3 (Jun-26) <strong>-0.89% miss</strong>, ending a beat streak. Fact · Yahoo.</li>\n<li><strong>Institutional 13F data: not available in feed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Insiders:</strong> Mostly sales — Newstead (2x sales), Levinson (grant+sale pattern, net seller), Borders, Parekh sales; no meaningful open-market buying visible. Modest bearish signal, though consistent with routine 10b5-1 exercise activity. Fact · Yahoo.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>MOAT AND MANAGEMENT</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Moat:</strong> Ecosystem lock-in + brand + Services attach (App Store, Wallet) — durable but growth-rate moat, not margin-expansion moat; net margin flat-to-high already (27.6%).</li>\n<li><strong>Reinvestment runway:</strong> Foldable iPhone framed as <strong>$14B TAM opportunity</strong> (Morgan Stanley) — incremental, not transformative, vs. $500B revenue base. Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=0060d5e4656d7e596fec6320e9969925535286d8a15985494f4040f30cbca308\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Capital allocation:</strong> Minimal dividend, buyback trend unconfirmed this cycle — capital-return story less clear than historical Apple playbook; monitor next 10-Q for verification.</li>\n<li><strong>Management transition risk:</strong> John Ternus is new CEO (stock +2.6% on news), pay package $58M FY27 — leadership continuity untested at this scale. Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=239c51eee1e9d47f336905194889d95e6b66f42dc62afaec6687b64740379cc2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Disruption risk:</strong> Media framing Apple's AI strategy as an open question (\"8 days to answer the AI question\") ahead of the Sept iPhone event — this is the swing factor for the next re-rating. Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=b0a6c608189033e6f6c556545d32fd7d962026bd302223ecad40d4ecea3d8242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>THESIS VALIDATION</h2>\n<strong>Bull case:</strong>\n1. EPS YoY +29.13% far outpaces revenue +16.36% — margin/buyback leverage still working. Fact · Yahoo.\n2. Analyst trend skews bullish: 34 buy/strong-buy vs 15 hold, 4 sell. Fact · Yahoo (analystTrend, 09/01/26).\n3. Apple positioned as \"AI trade hedge\" amid broader AI-capex wobble — defensive quality bid. Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=2e2e11237e8c00fc0b86bed0b9caa99edc76fe23e781578a510a7b58c3fc1817\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a>.<p><strong>Bear case:</strong><br/>1. Fwd PE (39.6x) > trailing PE (34.4x) signals Street expects EPS deceleration next FY — valuation risk if growth doesn't reaccelerate.<br/>2. Insider sales cluster (5+ transactions, no buys) + unconfirmed buyback trend removes the historical support pillar for the multiple.</p><p><strong>Pre-mortem:</strong> If Oct 28 print shows revenue growth <10% and no AI-driven Services acceleration, multiple compresses toward peer average (~25-28x), implying ~25-30% downside from here.</p><p><strong>Verdict: Neutral-to-Bearish near-term, Bullish long-term</strong> — quality compounder, wrong entry price today.</p><h2>SECTOR AND MACRO</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Macro feed unavailable</strong> — no rates/inflation/VIX data injected; cannot quantify multiple-compression risk from discount-rate moves.</li>\n<li>Sector: mega-cap tech near record highs on AI enthusiasm; Apple is a relative laggard in AI narrative vs MSFT/GOOGL/META (lower fwd growth optionality priced despite higher multiple).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>CATALYSTS AND RISKS</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Near-term:</strong> iPhone launch event ~1 week out (product-cycle catalyst). Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=7b1c61ebbcbda489f02d27036e53c78bcd5341d9dcfd19a087f318d5e480ce30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Next earnings: Oct 28, 2026, after the close (ET).</strong> Fact · <a class=\"src-link\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/calendar/earnings?symbol=AAPL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Earnings</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Risks:</strong> (1) AI strategy underwhelms at event → multiple de-rates; watch Services growth commentary. (2) CEO transition execution risk → watch guidance consistency. (3) Insider selling continues without offsetting buyback confirmation → watch next 10-Q capital-return disclosure.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>RETURN SCENARIOS (12-yr lens; benchmark: S&P500 ~9-10%/yr historical)</h2>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Prob</th><th>12-mo Target</th><th>12-yr CAGR (illustrative)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bear</td><td>25%</td><td>$270 (-17%)</td><td>~4% (multiple compresses to 25x, mid-single rev growth)</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>50%</td><td>$350 (+8%)</td><td>~8% (rev growth ~8-10%/yr, modest buyback aid)</td></tr><tr><td>Bull</td><td>25%</td><td>$410 (+26%)</td><td>~12% (AI monetization drives 12%+ rev growth, multiple holds)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul><li>Prob-weighted 12-mo return ≈ <strong>+6%</strong>. Dividend (0.5% yield) adds negligible compounding; buyback contribution <strong>unconfirmed</strong> this cycle — most 12-yr return must come from EPS growth, not shrinkage or yield. Versus S&P500 benchmark, base case underperforms; only bull case clears an above-market bar.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>ACTION PLAN</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Entry:</strong> 1/3 tranche at $290, 1/3 at $270, 1/3 at $255 — average toward buy-zone floor.</li>\n<li><strong>Add trigger:</strong> Q4 FY26/Q1 FY27 revenue reaccelerates >15% with Services margin expansion.</li>\n<li><strong>Trim/kill trigger:</strong> Two consecutive EPS misses, or confirmed shrinking buyback pace combined with fwd PE staying >38x.</li>\n<li><strong>KPIs to track:</strong> (1) Revenue growth vs 16.36% base, (2) Services growth rate, (3) Buyback/share-count trend (currently unknown — verify next filing), (4) Gross margin trend vs 48.65%, (5) iPhone event AI feature reception.</li>\n<li><strong>Alternative if not Buy:</strong> MSFT (27.7x PE, similar quality, cheaper) or GOOGL (17.3x PE, cheapest mega-cap growth multiple in peer set) for fresh growth capital today.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>SUMMARY</h2>\n<ul><li>Quality compounder, but priced for perfection at 34-40x earnings with a decelerating fwd EPS signal.</li>\n<li>EPS growth (+29%) outrunning revenue (+16%) — leverage intact, but capital-return support (buybacks) unconfirmed in this data.</li>\n<li>New CEO (Ternus) + Sept iPhone event are the swing catalysts for the next re-rating, up or down.</li>\n<li>Insider selling cluster with zero buys is a soft caution flag heading into the event.</li>\n<li>No prior report on file — first coverage, no drift to note.</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Scorecard:</strong> Growth: 7/10 | Moat: 8/10 | Management: 6/10 (transition risk) | Valuation: 3/10 | Balance sheet: 8/10 | Catalysts: 6/10 | <strong>Overall: 6/10</strong><p><strong>Outlook:</strong> 12-month: Hold/rangebound. 5-year: Likely market-perform if AI story doesn't materially reaccelerate growth. 12-year: Above-market only if entered near buy-zone; at current price, base case underperforms benchmark.</p><p>*Not investment advice — for informational purposes only.*</p>"}

event: companies
